// @contract: C-238
// #1400, the load-bearing cell, ALONE in its own file: 4294967294 iterations
// exhausted the general tree-walker's fuel budget by construction, so this was
// the corpus's one ledgered reference abstention (split off so the sibling
// guard rails in range_bind_no_materialize.almd kept their third vote). The
// reference now votes here through its registerized integer-loop tier — every
// iteration still executes, at a cost the totality gate can afford — and the
// abstain ledger is empty.
//
// A `let`-bound range used only as a `for-in` head is not materialized. A
// materializing leg needs ~32 GB for the block; a counting leg needs two locals.
// Before #1400 the wasm leg materialized (#1272's fix) while native iterated
// lazily, so this printed the sum natively and died `Error: out of memory` on
// wasm — found by the 2026-08-13 fuzz-nightly (run 31667874852, seed
// 506685997633 index 522). 0 + 1 + ... + 4294967293 = 9223372030412324865,
// which is representable in i64 (it is 942 short of 2^63-1).
effect fn main() -> Unit = {
  let huge = 0..<4294967295
  var hs = 0
  for i in huge {
    hs = hs + i
  }
  println("huge=" + int.to_string(hs))
}
